            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of β-Amino Ketones by Addition of Aryl Methyl Ketones to Sulfinimines: Application to the Total Synthesis of HPA-12, Norsedamine, and Sedamine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13488-13499</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.7b02611</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Synthesis of β-sulfinamido ketones was accomplished by the addition of silyl enol ethers derived from arylmethyl ketones to chiral sulfinimines in excellent yield and selectivity. Application of the formed β-amino substituted ketones is exemplified in the total synthesis of sphingolipid HPA-12 and the sedamine alkaloids.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
